{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795128324757,"sessionID":"ses_e0a0e9139ffeueffAzFzUVtP7e","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-86f383e6097f30be","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /travail && for f in 027 036 052 060; do echo ==================DOC-$f; cat /tmp/txt/doc-$f.txt; done"},"output":"==================DOC-027\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2025-2847\nPrinted on 13/08/2025\n1 / 3\nSERVICE REPORT\nInspection and maintenance\nReport reference :\nNC-RI-2025-2847\nPO number :\nPO-441115\nJob no. :\nAFF-42361\nCustomer :\nKeslor Laboratories, Head office:\nWexford\nSite :\nLivingston Plant\nInstallation :\nLine 1, piston filler\nEquipment :\nNevnis 160\nSerial number :\nplate missing\nAsset no. :\nINV-94287\nRequest date :\n27/07/2025\nIssue date :\n01/08/2025\nBackground and equipment\nNo leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 1. It is driven by a Vexlix\nmotor, type K64-4P. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nCourse of the visit\nThe maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook. The visit took place on 31 July 2025, following a request of 27\nJuly 2025. The customer's head office is in Wexford.\nReadings\nParameter\nValue\nDose volume, as found, E1-E3\n4'570 ; 4'590 ; 4'670\nDose volume, as left, E1-E3\n5'050 ; 5'100 ; 5'090\nDose volume, mean as left\n5'080\nFlow rate, as found\n103.8\nFlow rate, as left\n—\nOperating pressure, as found\n2.1\nOperating pressure, as left\n2.5\nProduct temperature (°C)\n29.8\nRating\nValue\nNominal volume\n5'000 µL\nTolerance\n± 2.5 %\nModel range (OEM)\n5 – 500 mL\nTank capacity\n50 L\nLine volume\n351 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 20 µL\nMax. flow\n297.6 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n8.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n4.2 bar\nAdjustments and results\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work started. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged\n4'610 µL.\nReplacements\nThe equipment runs on two shifts, five days a week, for liquid product packaging. Part VE-590-D (return spring) was inspected\nand found in good condition. Operators reported short stoppages at shift start, with no alarm message.\nDiagram\n\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2025-2847\nPrinted on 13/08/2025\n2 / 3\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprobe thermometer\nVexlix\nIN-49422\n21/03/2025\nreference pressure\ngauge\nVarevex\nET-84398\n06/06/2025\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nVE-761-B\ncheck valve\nreplaced\n393.03 €\nVE-590-D\nreturn spring\ninspected, kept\n169.20 €\nVE-111-C\ndosing nozzle\nordered (not fitted)\n272.34 €\nVE-324-E\npiston seal\nquoted\n44.75 €\nField team\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. Daniel Whitfield led the visit with the support of Declan Calloway,\nat the request of Grace Gallagher. Machine safety labels are legible and complete.\nTechnician's opinion\nThe previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid circuit. Tests were run until readings were stable. PLC settings were\nnot changed during the visit.\nApproval workflow\nThe manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date. The report was reviewed on 1 August 2025.\nNotes\nFor the record, manufacturer: Vergen.\nNote, status: Compliant.\nThe upstream conveyor Calanquin C63 (flow 307.8 L/h, pressure 4.6 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air\nnetwork runs at 7.0 bar.\nReport prepared by Declan Calloway.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 31/07/2026.\n\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2025-2847\nPrinted on 13/08/2025\n3 / 3\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: James Thornley\n==================DOC-036\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2026-5499\nOUTCOME\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSheet 1/4\nPrinted on May 7, 2026\nVisit record\nREPORT REFERENCE\nFT-RI-2026-5499\nPO NUMBER\nPO-209504\nJOB NO.\nAFF-12353\nCUSTOMER\nTalra Pharma, Head office: Wrexham\nINSTALLATION\nLine 1, automatic pipette\nOEM\nFenpax\nS/N\nFE-2018-64946\nASSET NO.\nINV-91362\nTOLERANCE\n± 0.1 cm³\nREQUEST DATE\nApril 16, 2026\nISSUE DATE\nApril 23, 2026\nDATE OF INTERVENTION\nApril 21, 2026\nReadings summary\n(provisional)\nDelivered volume\n5.01 cm³\nBackground and equipment\nFrame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion\nwas found. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nThe visit concerns the automatic pipette Drainvan 300. It is driven\nby a Fengen motor, type M105-4P. Sensor wiring was inspected\nand connectors tightened. Cleaning-in-place instructions were\nreminded to the production team.\nCourse of the visit\nMachine noise level in operation remained as usual. PLC settings\nwere not changed during the visit. Production data from recent\nweeks was reviewed with the customer. The visit to the customer,\nCarlow Plant, follows a request of 16 April 2026. The customer's\nhead office is in Wrexham. Checks were carried out with\ncalibrated instruments; certificates are available to the customer.\n\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2026-5499\nSheet 2/4\nPrinted on May 7, 2026\nReadings\nDelivered volume\nDelivery rate\nOperating\npressure\nAs found\n4.62\n25\n0.5\nE1\n5.01\n·\n·\nE2\n5.06\n·\n·\nE3\n5.05\n·\n·\nAs left\n5.04\n27\n—\nTol.\nReadings table units: doses in cm³, flow in mL/min, pressure in bar,\ntemperature in °C.\nMeasurement table values prevail; the summary shows provisional readings.\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n0.5 – 5 mL\nTank capacity\n2 L\nLine volume\n8 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.03 cm³\nMax. flow\n50 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n2.0 bar\nRelief valve s